# Titanic Classification — Model Evaluation & Hyperparameter Tuning

## Overview

This project was completed as part of the **Neurofive Solutions – Machine Learning Internship Track**.

The objective of this task was to evaluate a Titanic classification model using performance metrics beyond accuracy and to systematically tune the model using hyperparameter optimization.

A Logistic Regression model was evaluated using Precision, Recall, and F1-score. GridSearchCV was then used to tune the model's hyperparameters and compare the tuned model with the original baseline model.

---

## Objectives

The main objectives of this project were to:

- Evaluate the classification model beyond accuracy
- Calculate Precision, Recall, and F1-score
- Understand why accuracy alone can be misleading
- Apply hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV
- Tune multiple Logistic Regression hyperparameters
- Compare the original and tuned models
- Analyze whether tuning improved model performance

---

## Dataset

The project uses the **Titanic - Machine Learning from Disaster** dataset.

